  "question": {
    "text": "An element undergoes a reaction as shown :<br />\r<br />\r<math> <mrow> <mtext>X</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mtext>e</mtext> <mo>-</mo> </msup> <mo>→</mo> <msup> <mtext>X</mtext> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>-</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>, energy released <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>.87</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>eV</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>atom</mi></math>. If the energy released is used to dissociate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gms</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;molecules, equally into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is excited state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> atoms where the electron travels in orbit whose circumference equal to four times its de Broglie's wavelength. Determine the least moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> that would be required:<br />\r<br />\rGiven: I.E. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.6</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>eV</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>atom</mi></math> bond energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.526</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>eV</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>molecule</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
